7px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The E.U. hinges on=
 deep, dense legal and procedural rules, built over decades by a group of n=
ations that ceded sovereignty to one another, and to an unelected executive=
 branch in Brussels.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,se=
rif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Bringing in a country an ocean away i=
s not straightforward.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,=
serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Canada does not actually qualify fo=
r full E.U. membership, since, ultimately, it=E2=80=99s not in Europe. But =
bringing it closer to the E.U. is still complicated. And the initiative beg=
an raising eyebrows within minutes of being announced on the floor of the E=
uropean Parliament.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,ser=
if;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The issue was the name. The label the =
European Union wants to confer on Canada, =E2=80=9Cassociate member,=E2=80=
=9D is not an existing type of partnership. It has no obvious legal basis, =
and it=E2=80=99s not entirely clear what it would even entail.</span></p><p=
 style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><=
span>The term has drawn consternation from several member states, who see i=
t as vague, untethered from legal frameworks and potentially unfair to coun=
tries that already have detailed legal agreements with the E.U. That includ=
es candidate nations such as Albania and also Britain and Norway, who have =
deep trade and defense ties to the bloc.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal =
17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Some in Canada do=
n=E2=80=99t appear to love it either. The Conservative opposition leader se=
ized on the term, arguing that if Canada was to never be the 51st state of =
the U.S., it should also not become the 28th member state of the E.U.</span=
></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 =
15px"><span>Hours after von der Leyen spoke, the incoming Canadian ambassad=
or to the E.U. said that Canada preferred =E2=80=9Calliance for the future=
=E2=80=9D to describe the emerging new bond with the E.U. =E2=80=9CI think =
we=E2=80=99re still a ways away from actually landing on what we think the =
best way to describe it is,=E2=80=9D he said.</span></p><table border=3D"0"=
